note count_trap3: count checks its slice as read and write do, n <= len A and off <= len A - n, before it
note reads a byte; here off 5 and n 4 end one past an 8-byte array, so it traps 3, exit 103, whatever v is
om2
text before "before\n"
fn main to int
k = write 1 before 0 len before
a = new uchar 8 10
o = ulong 5
n = count a o 4 10
ret int n
end
